Our French plumber gave up plumbing a year ago, for what I always suspected were existentialist reasons. I imagined he had come to regard the systemic philosophy of plumbing as inauthentic, and had grown weary of extracting meaning from futility. This theory was based entirely on the fact that he's French, and therefore shrugged a lot and pronounced "system" in a way that seemed freighted with significance.
