"Is it fixed?" the boy asks.
"No," I say.
"Where's my reward?" he says.
"For what?"
"For helping you."
"Your reward," I say, "is a lesson in failure. We've failed."
A week later, my wife hears of a highly recommended plumber. He turns up a week after that, when I am home alone. Within half an hour, he is calling to me from the landing. "I found the problem," he says.
"Really?" I say. "That was quick."
"There was a load of scale and sludge stuck in your pump."
"Yes, I did think..."
"I got it going again, though," he says. "It's working fine now."
"But how did..."
