Holder also dances with BRB (he played a brilliantly bored chap in Ashton's Façade). For Quatrain, he picked a Piazzolla score, arranged by Leonid Desyatnikov and excitingly played live, and responds to its bite and languor. Adam Wiltshire's nest of steel trapeziums throws shadows against the wall, and four shirtless men drive the piece – the women embellish or curl up against them. Couples wind through ominous strings, especially in a solemn, faltering duet for Céline Gittens and Yasuo Atsuji. They bring a grown-up sense of melancholy, their haughty lines etching the air.
